From 72132d3116278884a22557e22e605dbee863b2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:52:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skins): encode current Bedrock skin packets

PlayerSkinPacket uses varint list lengths, numeric persona enums, UUID pack IDs, and fixed-width colors. Preserve the trailing trust fields so decoded skins can be sent back without discarding them. This enables connected skin changes and prevents malformed packets.

Transport complete SkinData to advertised Java clients with a versioned,
fragmented player_skin channel. Reuse the target protocol codec to preserve
all RGBA images, animation metadata, cape and geometry fields, persona
pieces and colors, flags, trust, and profile hash on direct and proxy routes.
Retain ordered immutable snapshots during configuration and flush after
Java join and capability registration. Keep legacy utility clients working.

Bound transport and negotiation memory explicitly, allocate received bytes
only as they arrive, and discard partial transfers on replacement or close.
Check list counts against remaining packet bytes before allocating and use
long image dimension products to reject overflow. Tests cover full classic
and persona records above five MiB, payload bounds, sequencing, lifecycle,
late negotiation, failed delivery, and malformed native fields.

The target server capture includes a player-list packet before StartGame.
Retain early player-list and skin packets in order until Java join, then
replay them through the normal handlers without reapplying base protocols.
This preserves initial profiles as well as their appearances and retains
removal and replacement semantics. Other pre-join packets are unchanged.

Carry local-player ownership in each fragment. ViaProxy's Java login UUID
can differ from the Bedrock actor UUID, so UUID-only installation misses
the local avatar even though every skin field arrived. Establish ownership
from the current actor unique ID or login identity and retain it through
fragment assembly. Add player-list identity before calling the provider.
